#!RuleTest
#test PMDA-SD2270 expect=skipped domain=DO
#note "DO declared class=FINDINGS is in Classes.Include, so ONLY the Domains.Exclude [DO] rejects. Pins this rule's unique sheet-given exclusion ('FINDINGS (-DO)', retained per the SD1202 ruling) - the deliberate counterpart of PMDA-SD1250-invalid_do_in_scope-DO, where the same-shaped dataset RUNS because SD1250's DO token was ruled away."
#library standard=sdtmig version=3-4
dataset DO class=FINDINGS label="Device Properties"
col STUDYID  type=Char
col DOMAIN   type=Char
col SPDEVID  type=Char
col DOSEQ    type=Num
col DOTESTCD type=Char
col DODY     type=Num
---
S1 | DO | DEV01 | 1 | DEVTYPE | 3
---
